    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0217" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 811.001/14: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-10T19:00:00+00:00"
                            >December 10, 1918—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My December 9, 10 p.m. The Foreign Office desires to receive if possible an
                    advance copy of President Wilson’s reply
                    to President Poincaré’s address, also to
                    know whether it will be delivered in French.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
